## 3. Complete 10-Step System Workflow (Section 9B)

1. **Zero-Typing Plot Onboarding:** The farmer opens the mobile web app (or WhatsApp bot), shares their GPS location (or selects their plot on the village satellite map / enters a mock [AgriStack UFSI](https://creuto.com/agristack-api-ufsi-farmer-registry-agritech) Farmer ID), selects their crop (`Paddy`, `Wheat`, `Cotton`, or `Maize`), and picks the sowing/transplanting week.
2. **Automated Geospatial & Soil Retrieval:** The backend queries **ISRIC SoilGrids (250m)** and district/village **Soil Health Card** baselines to auto-fill `pH`, `Soil Organic Carbon (SOC)`, `Clay/Sand/Silt %`, and baseline `N, P, K` status—requiring zero manual lab numbers from the farmer (though the farmer can override them if they have a printed Soil Health Card).
3. **All-Weather Satellite Time-Series Ingestion:** For the plot's 10m×10m bounding box from sowing date to current day, the system retrieves:
   * **Sentinel-2 L2A Optical Indices:** **SAVI** (Soil-Adjusted Vegetation Index for early Day-81 yield trajectory per [IJISAE](https://ijisae.org/index.php/IJISAE/article/view/2326)), **NDMI** (Normalized Difference Moisture Index for canopy water stress), and **NDRE** (Normalized Difference Red-Edge for chlorophyll/nitrogen status).
   * **Sentinel-1 C-Band SAR Fallback:** When cloud cover exceeds 30%, the pipeline fuses `VV` and `VH` radar backscatter and the Radar Vegetation Index (`RVI`) so monsoon cloud cover never blinds the model ([MDPI SAR Fusion](https://www.mdpi.com/2072-4292/17/8/1412)).
4. **Agro-Meteorological & Forecast Ingestion:** Retrieves cumulative season weather (`Growing Degree Days (GDD)`, cumulative rainfall, solar radiation, vapor pressure deficit) from **NASA POWER** and the **next 7 days of hourly/daily precipitation probability, wind speed, and reference evapotranspiration ($ET_0$)** from **Open-Meteo / IMD**.
5. **Input Completeness Check & Conformal Uncertainty Calibration:** An input validator checks which modalities are exact vs. imputed. If local soil test data or recent optical passes are missing, the system flags a **Data Completeness Score** and adjusts the conformal prediction intervals accordingly.
6. **Hybrid Yield Prediction (`P10 / P50 / P90`):** A two-stage **CatBoost/XGBoost + Temporal Feature Engine** predicts the baseline district-calibrated yield and applies a pixel-level `SAVI/NDMI` anomaly multiplier to output:
   * **P10 (Downside Risk Yield):** e.g., `18.2 Quintals/Acre` (if upcoming weather stress is unmanaged)
   * **P50 (Expected Median Yield):** e.g., `22.4 Quintals/Acre`
   * **P90 (Optimized Potential Yield):** e.g., `25.1 Quintals/Acre`
7. **Agronomic Stress & Waste Diagnosis:** The engine evaluates three real-time physical budgets:
   * **Root-Zone Water Balance:** Current `NDMI` + 7-day $\sum (Rain - ET_c)$.
   * **Urea Leaching & Volatilization Risk:** Probability of $>20\text{ mm}$ rain within 48 hours of top-dressing or soil moisture saturation.
   * **Phenological Sensitivity Weight ($K_y$):** Whether the crop is at a stress-critical stage (e.g., panicle initiation / flowering) or a tolerant stage.
8. **Counterfactual Action Simulation ("What-If" Engine):** The optimizer simulates 3 concrete 7-day schedules (e.g., **Option A: Routine Action Today**, **Option B: AI-Recommended 4-Day Delay + Split Dose**, **Option C: Do Nothing**) and computes for each option:
   * Expected Yield impact ($\Delta\text{ Quintals/Acre}$)
   * Water consumed vs. saved ($\text{Litres/Acre}$)
   * Fertilizer absorbed vs. leached ($\text{kg Urea wasted}$)
   * **Net Financial Gain (`₹ Saved + ₹ Yield Protected`)**
9. **Explainable UI & Vernacular Voice Delivery:** The farmer sees a simple traffic-light **Action Card** (*"HOLD IRRIGATION & DELAY UREA BY 4 DAYS — Saves ₹1,350 & 1.1 Lakh Litres/Acre"*) backed by a 1-tap **Telugu / Hindi / English audio button** and WhatsApp voice note summary.
10. **Closed-Loop Post-Harvest Feedback:** At harvest, the farmer or FPO logs actual harvested bags/quintals, updating regional calibration weights for the next season.

